IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sfa-periods`

-- Tests for sfa-periods.l4. Every expected value is worked out by hand from the calendar and the convention
-- written in sfa-periods.l4 (P1 to P10), and written beside its assertion. Both sides of each last day are tested,
-- with a start on the 31st and on 29 February.
-- 2024 is a leap year; 2025, 2026 and 2023 are not; 2100 is not (divisible by 100, not by 400).

§ `Days (P1)`

-- 31 Jan 2025 + 30 days: 28 days to reach 28 Feb, then 2 more = 2 Mar 2025.
#ASSERT `period: the last day of a period after` (Date 31 1 2025) 30 Days EQUALS Date 2 3 2025
-- 29 Feb 2024 + 365 days = 28 Feb 2025 (366 days would be 1 Mar 2025).
#ASSERT `period: the last day of a period after` (Date 29 2 2024) 365 Days EQUALS Date 28 2 2025
#ASSERT `period: the last day of a period after` (Date 29 2 2024) 366 Days EQUALS Date 1 3 2025
-- Start on the 31st, inside a month: 31 Aug 2025 + 14 = 14 Sep 2025.
#ASSERT `period: the last day of a period after` (Date 31 8 2025) 14 Days EQUALS Date 14 9 2025
-- A period of nought days ends the day of the event.
#ASSERT `period: the last day of a period after` (Date 31 8 2025) 0 Days EQUALS Date 31 8 2025
-- Across a year end: 20 Dec 2025 + 14 = 3 Jan 2026.
#ASSERT `period: the last day of a period after` (Date 20 12 2025) 14 Days EQUALS Date 3 1 2026

§ `Weeks (P3)`

-- 29 Feb 2024 + 2 weeks = 14 Mar 2024.
#ASSERT `period: the last day of a period after` (Date 29 2 2024) 2 Weeks EQUALS Date 14 3 2024
-- 31 Jan 2025 + 1 week = 7 Feb 2025.
#ASSERT `period: the last day of a period after` (Date 31 1 2025) 1 Weeks EQUALS Date 7 2 2025

§ `Months (P4): corresponding date, clamped to a short month`

-- 31 Aug 2025 + 6 months: no 31 Feb 2026, so 28 Feb 2026.
#ASSERT `period: the last day of a period after` (Date 31 8 2025) 6 Months EQUALS Date 28 2 2026
-- 31 Jan 2024 + 1 month: 2024 is a leap year, so 29 Feb 2024.
#ASSERT `period: the last day of a period after` (Date 31 1 2024) 1 Months EQUALS Date 29 2 2024
-- 31 Jan 2025 + 1 month: 28 Feb 2025.
#ASSERT `period: the last day of a period after` (Date 31 1 2025) 1 Months EQUALS Date 28 2 2025
-- 29 Feb 2024 + 12 months: no 29 Feb 2025, so 28 Feb 2025.
#ASSERT `period: the last day of a period after` (Date 29 2 2024) 12 Months EQUALS Date 28 2 2025
-- 29 Feb 2024 + 48 months: 29 Feb 2028 exists.
#ASSERT `period: the last day of a period after` (Date 29 2 2024) 48 Months EQUALS Date 29 2 2028
-- 30 Nov 2025 + 3 months: 28 Feb 2026.
#ASSERT `period: the last day of a period after` (Date 30 11 2025) 3 Months EQUALS Date 28 2 2026
-- 31 Mar 2025 + 1 month: 30 Apr 2025.
#ASSERT `period: the last day of a period after` (Date 31 3 2025) 1 Months EQUALS Date 30 4 2025
-- A month whose corresponding date exists is not clamped: 15 Jan 2025 + 1 month = 15 Feb 2025.
#ASSERT `period: the last day of a period after` (Date 15 1 2025) 1 Months EQUALS Date 15 2 2025
-- Across a year end: 31 Dec 2025 + 2 months = 28 Feb 2026.
#ASSERT `period: the last day of a period after` (Date 31 12 2025) 2 Months EQUALS Date 28 2 2026

§ `Years (P4)`

-- 29 Feb 2024 + 1 year: 28 Feb 2025.
#ASSERT `period: the last day of a period after` (Date 29 2 2024) 1 Years EQUALS Date 28 2 2025
-- 29 Feb 2024 + 4 years: 29 Feb 2028.
#ASSERT `period: the last day of a period after` (Date 29 2 2024) 4 Years EQUALS Date 29 2 2028
-- 31 Dec 2025 + 1 year: 31 Dec 2026.
#ASSERT `period: the last day of a period after` (Date 31 12 2025) 1 Years EQUALS Date 31 12 2026

§ `The window "within N units after X" and "not later than" (P2): both sides of the last day`

-- Event 31 Jan 2025, 30 days: the last day is 2 Mar 2025.
#ASSERT `period: the date is within a period after` (Date 31 1 2025) (Date 1 2 2025) 30 Days EQUALS TRUE       -- the first day of the window
#ASSERT `period: the date is within a period after` (Date 31 1 2025) (Date 2 3 2025) 30 Days EQUALS TRUE       -- the last day
#ASSERT `period: the date is within a period after` (Date 31 1 2025) (Date 3 3 2025) 30 Days EQUALS FALSE      -- the day after the last day
#ASSERT `period: the date is within a period after` (Date 31 1 2025) (Date 31 1 2025) 30 Days EQUALS FALSE     -- the day of the event is not after it (P2)
#ASSERT `period: the date is within a period after` (Date 31 1 2025) (Date 30 1 2025) 30 Days EQUALS FALSE     -- before the event
-- "Not later than": an early act is in time; the day after the last day is not.
#ASSERT `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` (Date 31 1 2025) (Date 31 1 2025) 30 Days EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` (Date 31 1 2025) (Date 30 1 2025) 30 Days EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` (Date 31 1 2025) (Date 2 3 2025) 30 Days EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` (Date 31 1 2025) (Date 3 3 2025) 30 Days EQUALS FALSE
-- Months, start on 29 Feb 2024, 12 months: last day 28 Feb 2025.
#ASSERT `period: the date is within a period after` (Date 29 2 2024) (Date 28 2 2025) 12 Months EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `period: the date is within a period after` (Date 29 2 2024) (Date 1 3 2025) 12 Months EQUALS FALSE
-- Months, start on 31 Aug 2025, 6 months: last day 28 Feb 2026.
#ASSERT `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` (Date 31 8 2025) (Date 28 2 2026) 6 Months EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` (Date 31 8 2025) (Date 1 3 2026) 6 Months EQUALS FALSE

§ `A period before an event (P5, P6)`

-- 14 days before 20 Oct 2026 is 6 Oct 2026.
#ASSERT `period: the latest day for an act a period before` (Date 20 10 2026) 14 Days EQUALS Date 6 10 2026
-- Across a month end: 14 days before 5 Mar 2024 is 20 Feb 2024 (2024 has a 29 Feb).
#ASSERT `period: the latest day for an act a period before` (Date 5 3 2024) 14 Days EQUALS Date 20 2 2024
-- 2 weeks before 29 Feb 2024 is 15 Feb 2024.
#ASSERT `period: the latest day for an act a period before` (Date 29 2 2024) 2 Weeks EQUALS Date 15 2 2024
-- 8 months before 31 Oct 2025: no 31 Feb 2025, so 28 Feb 2025.
#ASSERT `period: the latest day for an act a period before` (Date 31 10 2025) 8 Months EQUALS Date 28 2 2025
-- 1 month before 31 Mar 2025 is 28 Feb 2025.
#ASSERT `period: the latest day for an act a period before` (Date 31 3 2025) 1 Months EQUALS Date 28 2 2025
-- 1 year before 29 Feb 2024 is 28 Feb 2023.
#ASSERT `period: the latest day for an act a period before` (Date 29 2 2024) 1 Years EQUALS Date 28 2 2023
-- Both sides of the latest day: an act 14 days before 20 Oct 2026 is on 6 Oct (in), 7 Oct (out).
#ASSERT `period: the date is at least a period before` (Date 6 10 2026) (Date 20 10 2026) 14 Days EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `period: the date is at least a period before` (Date 7 10 2026) (Date 20 10 2026) 14 Days EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `period: the date is at least a period before` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 20 10 2026) 14 Days EQUALS TRUE
-- Within 6 months before 31 Aug 2026: from 28 Feb 2026 up to 30 Aug 2026.
#ASSERT `period: the date is within a period before` (Date 28 2 2026) (Date 31 8 2026) 6 Months EQUALS TRUE   -- first day
#ASSERT `period: the date is within a period before` (Date 27 2 2026) (Date 31 8 2026) 6 Months EQUALS FALSE  -- day before the first day
#ASSERT `period: the date is within a period before` (Date 30 8 2026) (Date 31 8 2026) 6 Months EQUALS TRUE   -- last day
#ASSERT `period: the date is within a period before` (Date 31 8 2026) (Date 31 8 2026) 6 Months EQUALS FALSE  -- the day of the event itself

§ `Clear days (P7)`

-- 14 clear days before 20 Oct 2026: neither 20 Oct nor the day of the act is counted, so the latest day is 5 Oct.
#ASSERT `period: the latest day for an act at least a number of clear days before` (Date 20 10 2026) 14 EQUALS Date 5 10 2026
-- Across 29 Feb: 1 clear day before 1 Mar 2024 is 28 Feb 2024.
#ASSERT `period: the latest day for an act at least a number of clear days before` (Date 1 3 2024) 1 EQUALS Date 28 2 2024
-- After 14 clear days from 20 Oct 2026: the earliest day is 4 Nov 2026.
#ASSERT `period: the earliest day for an act after a number of clear days from` (Date 20 10 2026) 14 EQUALS Date 4 11 2026
-- From 31 Jan 2025, 28 clear days: earliest 1 Mar 2025 (31 Jan + 28 = 28 Feb, plus 1).
#ASSERT `period: the earliest day for an act after a number of clear days from` (Date 31 1 2025) 28 EQUALS Date 1 3 2025

§ `Calendar months`

#ASSERT `period: the last day of the calendar month containing` (Date 15 2 2025) EQUALS Date 28 2 2025
#ASSERT `period: the last day of the calendar month containing` (Date 29 2 2024) EQUALS Date 29 2 2024
#ASSERT `period: the last day of the calendar month containing` (Date 1 2 2024) EQUALS Date 29 2 2024
#ASSERT `period: the last day of the calendar month containing` (Date 31 8 2025) EQUALS Date 31 8 2025
#ASSERT `period: the last day of the calendar month containing` (Date 10 4 2025) EQUALS Date 30 4 2025

§ `Business days (P8)`

-- Fixtures. 1 Nov 2026 is a Sunday. So 2 to 6 Nov are Monday to Friday, 7 and 8 Nov are Saturday and Sunday, 9 Nov a Monday.
-- Here Monday 9 Nov 2026 is taken to be a public holiday. (An invented holiday: the Act lists none, and does not define "business day".)
`the supplied public holidays` MEANS LIST Date 9 11 2026
`no public holidays` MEANS EMPTY

#ASSERT `period: the date is a business day` (Date 2 11 2026) `the supplied public holidays` EQUALS TRUE     -- a Monday
#ASSERT `period: the date is a business day` (Date 6 11 2026) `the supplied public holidays` EQUALS TRUE     -- a Friday
#ASSERT `period: the date is a business day` (Date 7 11 2026) `the supplied public holidays` EQUALS FALSE    -- a Saturday
#ASSERT `period: the date is a business day` (Date 1 11 2026) `the supplied public holidays` EQUALS FALSE    -- a Sunday
#ASSERT `period: the date is a business day` (Date 9 11 2026) `the supplied public holidays` EQUALS FALSE    -- a Monday that is a public holiday
#ASSERT `period: the date is a business day` (Date 9 11 2026) `no public holidays` EQUALS TRUE                -- the same Monday where it is not
#ASSERT `period: the date is a business day` (Date 10 11 2026) `the supplied public holidays` EQUALS TRUE    -- the Tuesday after

-- 5 business days after Friday 6 Nov, with Monday 9 Nov a holiday: Tue 10, Wed 11, Thu 12, Fri 13, Mon 16 = 16 Nov.
#ASSERT `period: the last day of a number of business days after` (Date 6 11 2026) 5 `the supplied public holidays` EQUALS Date 16 11 2026
-- Without the holiday: Mon 9, Tue 10, Wed 11, Thu 12, Fri 13 = 13 Nov.
#ASSERT `period: the last day of a number of business days after` (Date 6 11 2026) 5 `no public holidays` EQUALS Date 13 11 2026
-- Starting on a Saturday (7 Nov), 1 business day, the Monday being a holiday: Tue 10 Nov.
#ASSERT `period: the last day of a number of business days after` (Date 7 11 2026) 1 `the supplied public holidays` EQUALS Date 10 11 2026
-- Nought business days ends the day of the event.
#ASSERT `period: the last day of a number of business days after` (Date 6 11 2026) 0 `the supplied public holidays` EQUALS Date 6 11 2026
-- Both sides of the last day (16 Nov): in on 16 Nov, out on 17 Nov, out on the day of the event.
#ASSERT `period: the date is within a number of business days after` (Date 6 11 2026) (Date 16 11 2026) 5 `the supplied public holidays` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `period: the date is within a number of business days after` (Date 6 11 2026) (Date 17 11 2026) 5 `the supplied public holidays` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `period: the date is within a number of business days after` (Date 6 11 2026) (Date 6 11 2026) 5 `the supplied public holidays` EQUALS FALSE
-- A calendar Saturday in the middle of the window is inside it: 7 Nov.
#ASSERT `period: the date is within a number of business days after` (Date 6 11 2026) (Date 7 11 2026) 5 `the supplied public holidays` EQUALS TRUE

§ `A period beginning with a day, and a period ending with a day (P10)`

-- "N units beginning with D": D is day 1. 15 Jan 2026 + 6 months = 15 Jul 2026; the day before is 14 Jul 2026.
#ASSERT `period: the last day of a period beginning with` (Date 15 1 2026) 6 Months EQUALS Date 14 7 2026
-- 31 Aug 2026 + 6 months clamps to 28 Feb 2027 (P4); stepping 28 Feb 2027 back 6 months gives 28 Aug, not 31 Aug, so the clamped date is the last day.
#ASSERT `period: the last day of a period beginning with` (Date 31 8 2026) 6 Months EQUALS Date 28 2 2027
-- 31 Dec 2026 + 6 months clamps to 30 Jun 2027; stepping back gives 30 Dec, not 31 Dec, so the last day is 30 Jun 2027.
#ASSERT `period: the last day of a period beginning with` (Date 31 12 2026) 6 Months EQUALS Date 30 6 2027
-- 28 Feb 2026 + 6 months = 28 Aug 2026 (no clamp; the round trip returns 28 Feb); the day before is 27 Aug 2026.
#ASSERT `period: the last day of a period beginning with` (Date 28 2 2026) 6 Months EQUALS Date 27 8 2026
-- days: 1 Jan 2026, 15 days: day 1 is 1 Jan, day 15 is 15 Jan 2026.
#ASSERT `period: the last day of a period beginning with` (Date 1 1 2026) 15 Days EQUALS Date 15 1 2026
-- weeks: 1 Jan 2026, 2 weeks (14 days): day 14 is 14 Jan 2026.
#ASSERT `period: the last day of a period beginning with` (Date 1 1 2026) 2 Weeks EQUALS Date 14 1 2026
-- years: 1 Mar 2026, 1 year: the day before 1 Mar 2027 is 28 Feb 2027.
#ASSERT `period: the last day of a period beginning with` (Date 1 3 2026) 1 Years EQUALS Date 28 2 2027

-- "N units ending with D": D is the last day. 15 days ending with 15 Jan 2026 begin on 1 Jan 2026.
#ASSERT `period: the first day of a period ending with` (Date 15 1 2026) 15 Days EQUALS Date 1 1 2026
-- 6 months ending with 30 Jun 2026: the period is 1 Jan to 30 Jun 2026 (the day after, 1 Jul, less 6 months, is 1 Jan).
#ASSERT `period: the first day of a period ending with` (Date 30 6 2026) 6 Months EQUALS Date 1 1 2026
-- 6 months ending with 28 Feb 2027: 1 Mar 2027 less 6 months is 1 Sep 2026.
#ASSERT `period: the first day of a period ending with` (Date 28 2 2027) 6 Months EQUALS Date 1 9 2026
-- weeks: 2 weeks ending with 14 Jan 2026 begin on 1 Jan 2026.
#ASSERT `period: the first day of a period ending with` (Date 14 1 2026) 2 Weeks EQUALS Date 1 1 2026

-- the two agree: the period beginning 1 Jan 2026 for 6 months ends 30 Jun 2026, and the period of 6 months ending then begins 1 Jan 2026.
#ASSERT `period: the first day of a period ending with` (`period: the last day of a period beginning with` (Date 1 1 2026) 6 Months) 6 Months EQUALS Date 1 1 2026
